# Change Control Checklist

Before finalizing changes to money/auth/security paths, confirm:

- Validation: amount, enum status, required fields, and finite-number checks are enforced.
- Authorization: route permission checks and role boundaries are unchanged or tightened.
- Security: no new bypasses for signature, replay protection, idempotency, or MFA.
- Observability: add or preserve audit events and actionable logs for failures.
- Error strategy: unexpected external/provider responses fail safe with explicit error.
- Lint/quality: run lints for edited files and fix newly introduced issues.

## Deployment Discipline

- Any migration affecting billing/wallet tables must include backward-safe defaults.
- Never rely on manual runtime setup when defaults can be encoded in migration + code.
- Document required env vars whenever auth/email/security behavior depends on them.
